## Scope

Workspace-cookie-cut companion to bd:JMAP-ayoz.40 (which closed the metadata-server destroy-array-element case).

Multiple extension-server handlers interpolate a `serde_json::Value` argument into an `invalid_arguments` description via Display. Examples (non-exhaustive):

```
crate-jmap-mail-server/src/mailbox.rs:142   position: ... got {v}
crate-jmap-mail-server/src/mailbox.rs:152   anchor: ... got {v}
crate-jmap-mail-server/src/mailbox.rs:159   anchorOffset: ... got {v}
crate-jmap-mail-server/src/sieve.rs:1028    position: ... got {v}
crate-jmap-mail-server/src/sieve.rs:1035    limit: ... got {v}
crate-jmap-mail-server/src/sieve.rs:1052    anchorOffset: ... got {v}
crate-jmap-chat-server/src/message.rs:147   position: ... got {v}
crate-jmap-chat-server/src/emoji.rs:139     position: ... got {v}
crate-jmap-chat-server/src/contact.rs:332   position: ... got {v}
crate-jmap-chat-server/src/space.rs:573     position: ... got {v}
crate-jmap-calendars-server/src/event.rs:800 position: ... got {v}
```

Plus likely the same pattern in tasks-server, contacts-server, filenode-server, sharing-server — full audit needed.

## Severity vs metadata-server

Lower than .40 because each call site interpolates a SCALAR argument from a known shallow field name (position / anchor / anchorOffset / limit). An attacker controls the JSON shape but the values are bounded by typical client behaviour — a 10MB `position` is unusual.

But the SAME defense-in-depth fix applies: emit only the JSON type tag, never the value.

## Fix shape

Same as .40 — a private helper or local match arm that renders just the type tag. Could be extracted into a shared helper in jmap-server if the workspace wants a single point of policy.

## Why P4

Hygiene, no behaviour change, no client visible. Bumps fixed by .40 closure; this is the propagation tail.

## Cross-references

- bd:JMAP-ayoz.40 (closed) — original metadata-server fix
- bd:JMAP-x2gd.93 / bd:JMAP-ayoz.39 — related but different (Id boundary validation, not error-message hygiene)

## Acceptance

- All call sites enumerated above audited
- Either fixed inline OR refactored to a shared helper in jmap-server
- Each fixed site carries the same rationale comment as the .40 metadata-server fix
- New oracle tests pin the no-leak property at one site per crate (no need to test every individual site)
- cargo test --workspace green
- cargo clippy --workspace -D warnings green
